  "string": "VERDICT: the crowding IV is an attempted design, not informative causal evidence. Under the honest specification (release_month + dow + subfield_kw FE, no day FE) the first stage is modest (t=-5.6, KP-F=31) and the weak-IV-robust AR 95% CI (0.021, 0.921) is 0.90 log-points wide, barely excludes zero and includes the OLS estimate (0.508). The day-FE first stage (KP-F=413) is the within-day adding-up identity, not exogenous variation (2SLS beta 0.917 in singleton cells vs 0.619 in non-singleton cells); a same-topic crowding instrument with no adding-up link to own upvotes (own-subfield leave-one-out peer sum, no day FE) has no usable first stage (t=-0.55). Report as 'consistent with OLS but uninformative'; do not describe as suggestive causal support.",
